.TH PAM_TPM_PIN 8 "November 2026" "tpm-pin 1.0.10" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pam_tpm_pin \- PAM authentication module for TPM 2.0 PIN login
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pam_tpm_pin.so
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pam_tpm_pin
is a Pluggable Authentication Module (PAM) that enables Windows Hello\-style
hardware-backed PIN authentication backed by a TPM 2.0 security processor.
.PP
It displays a unified prompt (\fB"PIN or Password: "\fP) when invoked for an
allowed local PAM service and an enrolled user. Input that matches the
configured PIN policy format is verified against the TPM 2.0 using AES-128-CFB
parameter transit encryption. Standard system passwords that do not match the
PIN format bypass the TPM completely and pass straight through to downstream
modules such as
.BR pam_unix (8)
(\fBtry_first_pass\fP) without consuming hardware Dictionary Attack attempts.
.PP
When a PIN succeeds and a login password was sealed at enrollment time,
.B pam_tpm_pin
sets \fBPAM_AUTHTOK\fP and the GNOME Keyring \fBgkr_system_authtok\fP data
item so desktop keyrings unlock automatically.
.SH SECURITY MODEL
.IP \(bu 2
Remote, network, and autologin PAM services (such as \fBsshd\fP,
\fBdropbear\fP, \fBtelnet\fP, \fBrlogin\fP, \fBcrond\fP, \fBcockpit\fP,
\fBxrdp\fP, \fBvnc\fP, and non-local \fBPAM_RHOST\fP connections) are
explicitly rejected and always return \fBPAM_IGNORE\fP.
.IP \(bu 2
Direct TPM device access (\fI/dev/tpmrm0\fP) remains restricted to \fBroot\fP.
Unprivileged screen lockers authenticate through the setuid-root
\fBtpm-pin-verify\fP helper, which never exposes unsealed keyring passwords to
unprivileged processes.
.IP \(bu 2
Scope flags (\fBenable_login\fP, \fBenable_lockscreen\fP, \fBenable_sudo\fP,
\fBenable_polkit\fP) restrict which local PAM services accept TPM PINs.
.IP \(bu 2
Credential blobs bind metadata header fields and target UID into AES-256-GCM
associated authenticated data (AAD).
.SH MODULE TYPES PROVIDED
.B pam_tpm_pin.so
provides \fBauth\fP authentication (\fBpam_sm_authenticate\fP,
\fBpam_sm_setcred\fP) and a passive \fBpassword\fP hook
(\fBpam_sm_chauthtok\fP on \fBPAM_UPDATE_AUTHTOK\fP) that flags sealed desktop
keyring credentials as stale when a user changes their login password, without
ever blocking password changes. All outcomes (success, failure, DA lockout,
PCR 7 mismatch, and stale-keyring events) are audited via
.BR pam_syslog (3)
to \fBLOG_AUTHPRIV\fP without logging secrets. Account and session hooks return
\fBPAM_IGNORE\fP.
.SH RETURN VALUES
.TP
.B PAM_SUCCESS
The user's PIN was verified by the TPM 2.0 hardware.
.TP
.B PAM_IGNORE
The service is disallowed, remote, disabled by configuration, or the user has
no enrolled PIN.
.TP
.B PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL
PIN verification failed or input did not match the PIN format; PAM falls back
to standard password authentication.
.TP
.B PAM_USER_UNKNOWN
Target username could not be resolved.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tpm-pin/config.conf
System policy and scope configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tpm-pin/<uid>/sealed.blob
Root-only TPM-sealed credential blob.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tpm-pin-ctl (1),
.BR pam (8),
.BR pam.conf (5)
